# Deterministic checkouts across platforms.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf setting decides what the working tree gets, so the same commit is LF on a
# Linux runner and CRLF on a Windows one. That difference is invisible until something hashes the bytes:
# a test fixture built from a raw string literal takes its line endings from the source file, and the
# release signature covers the checksum manifest byte for byte.
#
# The repository already stores LF in the index, so forcing LF on checkout changes nothing that is
# committed and keeps every platform reading the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted or merged as text.
*.onnx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.msi binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary

# Generated artifacts and lock files are diffed as text, but keep them out of merge conflicts.
packages.lock.json -merge
